Q: How to change text on the span use vue.js 2? A: <p>On the template you will change the span with:</p>

<pre><code>&lt;span v-if="totalNotif &gt; 0" class="badge" id="total-notif" v-text="totalNotif"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>This will connect <code>span</code> with value <code>totalNotif</code>.
So on VueJs part, remove jquery part, updating only data <code>totalNotif</code> and automatically will update span text content.</p>

<p>EDIT
To better understand, the script part become:</p>

<pre><code>export default {
    mounted() {
        this.initialMount()
    },

    data() {
       return {
          totalNotif: 0
       }
    },

    methods: {
        initialMount() {
            Echo.private('App.User.' + window.Laravel.authUser.id).notification((notification) =&gt; {
                this.totalNotif = this.totalNotif + 1

            })
        },
    }
}
</code></pre>
